Switch: skip the GL state calls a render pipeline change does not change (COS_SWITCH_GL_STATE_CACHE)

RenderPipeline::ApplyNow issued its whole fixed-function state on every SetPipeline: front face,
culling, depth test/mask/func, stencil ops and mask, sample mask, alpha to coverage, polygon
offset, and per color target blend enable, equations, factors and write mask, plus
glUseProgram (~25 calls; ~190 pipeline changes per Outset frame). Mesa compares most of them
with its own state, but each call still costs a dispatch, a context lookup and the comparison.
With the cache (default on; COS_SWITCH_GL_STATE_CACHE=0 for the old path) the render pass's
PersistentPipelineState remembers what the pipelines of the pass set and ApplyNowCached issues
only the calls whose value differs, glUseProgram included. A pass starts with nothing known (the
LoadOp clears and the default state run before its first command, and nothing else touches this
state inside a pass); the non-indexed draw-buffer path keeps the old code.

Checked with switch/dawn/gltest: pipelines that switch blend (additive, alpha, none), color
write masks, depth compare and write, cull mode and front face between draws give the same
pixels as the CPU reference with the cache off and on, and wrong ones when a cached depth mask or
write mask is not updated.
